# The Theorist, Jace Beleren's -2 is "up to one target" for each opponent, so it is activated with no target at all when no
# opponent controls an artifact or a creature (CR 115.1, 601.2c): Bot2 has only an Island. Bot1 activates it on turn 3, no
# target question is asked (the refusal), nothing returns, and the loyalty cost is paid (4 -> 2, CR 606.4). Jace's +1 on
# turn 1 (one loyalty ability a turn) leaves Bot1 its own Illusion, which is no target: only what an opponent controls is.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
The Theorist, Jace Beleren
Island x4
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Activate(Ability: +1)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Activate(Ability: For each opponent)
! Bot1.Target
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Illusion Token; Island; The Theorist, Jace Beleren
Bot1.Battlefield.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Counters.Loyalty = 2
Stack.Count = 0
